00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.240
The 
Shining is well known, not only for it’s

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:09.509
genius director, but also it’s unbelievable
performances from Jack Nicholson, Shelley

00:06:09.509 --> 00:06:12.050
Duvall, Danny Lloyd and Scatman Crothers.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:16.720
Doctor Sleep chose to recast these characters,
even though realistic visual effects now exist,

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.180
so the characters had to recreate the performances
of the actors in The Shining.

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:23.419
In the prologue, when Danny is talking to
Dick Halloran on the bench, Wendy comes up

00:06:23.419 --> 00:06:27.379
screaming Danny’s name, crying as if she
had been looking for him in a panic is a mimic

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.380
of the penultimate scene of the Shining.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.020
"Danny? Danny!"

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:34.060
"Mommy!"

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.900
"Danny! Danny!"

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:44.740
There’s also a facial expression that fans
have dubbed The Kubrick Stare, in which a

00:06:44.759 --> 00:06:49.169
character tilts their chin down while looking
up to make them look deviously sinister on

00:06:49.169 --> 00:06:50.169
camera.

00:06:50.169 --> 00:06:53.330
During the ambush scene, where Danny and Billy
hide out in the woods with rifles to take

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:57.509
down the nomads who are coming for Abra, the
last one standing is Snakebite Andi who emerges

00:06:57.509 --> 00:07:00.910
from the trailing donning the signature Kubrickian
look.

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:04.380
One of the scenes where Jack can be seen with
a creepy expression in the Shining is while

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:08.420
he’s staring at Wendy and Danny in the miniature
hedge maze, so I took it as no coincidence that

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:12.620
the town adult Danny ends up in also has a
miniature model version, that Danny spends

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.990
some time helping to build.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:17.400
It is here where he meets Billy, who introduces
him to the man he would interview with for

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:21.110
the job at the hospice, and that interview
takes place in a room that is identical to

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:24.270
the room Jack interviews in for the caretaker
job at the overlook.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:28.930
The wall color, layout, window placement,
this flag, that pen, the cup, the artwork

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:33.110
and even some of the camera angles used to
shoot it are a direct recreation of Jack’s

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:34.110
interview.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:36.780
For both characters, it represents a point
of no return in the story.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:39.840
Other parallels between Jack and Danny exist
up and down the plot.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.470
I mentioned the fact that they are both alcoholics,
and Danny brings this up during one of the

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:47.360
AA meetings, saying he’s standing where
his father once stood, and that idea comes

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:51.590
back when he and Rose face off in the Overlook’s
Colorado Lounge and he asks her if she knows

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:52.650
where she’s standing.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:56.800
The axe fight between Danny and Rose also
goes up and down the stairs, being blocked

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:01.370
out exactly how the fight between Jack and
Wendy went down nearly 40 years prior.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.699
But the connections to The Shining do not
end there.

00:08:03.699 --> 00:08:07.189
During the flashback, Wendy and Danny can
be seen watching a Bugs Bunny cartoon that

00:08:07.189 --> 00:08:10.430
illustrates the current state of affairs,
and connects to the shirt that Danny wore

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:12.099
in his first scene in the Shining.

00:08:12.099 --> 00:08:15.069
Bugs Bunny is chosen because Bugs’ catch
phrase is

00:08:15.069 --> 00:08:17.180
“What’s Up, Doc?”

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.220
And Danny’s nickname in The Shining is Doc…

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:25.360
Which carries over to current times where
Danny becomes known at the hospice as Doctor

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:26.370
Sleep.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:30.210
Before we move on from Danny, one other thing
I noticed was during the end credits.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:34.070
Danny Lloyd, the actor who played Danny Torrance
in The Shining was listed as “Spectator”.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.420
I’m guessing he may have made his cameo
at the movie theater or the little league

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:38.420
game.

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:42.070
Before Doctor Sleep, he hadn’t acted since
1982; but the spooky part is that after he

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:46.270
decided to quit acting he grew up and became
a teacher, just as Jack Torrance was in The

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.400
Shining.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.660
[spooky clip]

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:53.710
Unfortunately, one actor who could not have
come back to reprise his role was Scatman

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:55.780
Crothers who passed away in 1986.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:09:00.720
His character, Dick Halloran has a final conversation
with Danny in Doctor Sleep, where Danny describes

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:04.410
each of the ghosts of the Overlook’s past
that he’d locked away in Halloran’s box,

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:08.360
the last of which was Horace Derwent, who
spat out his signature phrase, “Great party,

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.530
isn’t it?” as the box locked him away.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:12.670
There are two Things You (might have) Missed
here.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:15.560
The guy he’s referring to seems to be this
guy from The Shining.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:18.000
“Great party, isn’t it?”

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:22.460
...who’s credited as “Injured Guest”,
and who I dressed up as for Halloween in 2012.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:26.400
The bald cap didn’t really work out, so
I ended up being a younger version of Injured

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:27.400
Guest.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:30.980
Doctor Sleep makes the suggestion that Injured
Guest is actually Horace Derwent, a character

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:33.440
from the history of the Overlook in the novel.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:37.370
Horace was a millionaire inventor, pilot,
film producer and entrepreneur who bought

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:41.940
and renovated the hotel in 1945 and turned
the place into an entertainment destination

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:44.250
as well as adding a roque court in the lawn.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:48.310
The Overlook was perhaps his one unsuccessful
business venture though, and he sold the property

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:50.220
after losing three million dollars on it.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:52.710
I guess that party wasn’t so great after
all.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:55.650
